ccruals":-0.006169956838604684,"_gp_accruals":true,"_score_accruals":60.0,"_gate_rev_volatility":0.1102673349783632,"_gp_rev_volatility":true,"_score_rev_volatility":82.8,"_gate_margin_vs_hist":0.042790619901217464,"_gp_margin_vs_hist":true,"_score_margin_vs_hist":46.5,"_gate_piotroski":5,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":55.6,"_gate_spread":null,"_gp_spread":null,"_score_spread":null,"_gate_roic_consistency":null,"_gp_roic_consistency":null,"_score_roic_consistency":null,"_gate_incr_roic":null,"_gp_incr_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":null,"_gp_margin_advantage":null,"_score_margin_advantage":null,"_gate_pool_share":0.06115447526939377,"_gp_pool_share":true,"_score_pool_share":64.5,"_gate_rev_durability":0.09964954239985446,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":74.8,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":-0.011467942999086855,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":0.0,"_gate_share_shrink":0.0422271739147424,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.0035145603213312293,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":94.1,"_gate_insider_own":0.0086199995,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":5.7,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Arthur J. Gallagher & Co., together with its subsidiaries, provides insurance and reinsurance brokerage, consulting, and third-party property/casualty claims settlement and administration services to entities and individuals worldwide. The company operates in Brokerage and Risk Management segments. Its Brokerage segment offers retail and wholesale insurance and reinsurance brokerage services; assists retail brokers and other non-affiliated brokers in the placement of specialized and hard-to-place insurance; and acts as a brokerage wholesaler, managing general agent, and managing general underwriter for distributing specialized insurance coverages to underwriting enterprises. This segment performs activities, including marketing, underwriting, issuing policies, collecting premiums, appointing and supervising other agents, paying claims, and negotiating reinsurance; and offers services in the areas of insurance and reinsurance placement, risk of loss management, and management of employer sponsored benefit programs. The Risk Management segment provides contract claim settlement and administration services; and claims management, loss control consulting, and insurance property appraisal services. The company offers its services through a network of correspondent brokers and consultants. It serves commercial, industrial, public, religious, and nonprofit entities, as well as underwriting enterprises. The company was founded in 1927 and is headquartered in Rolling Meadows, Illinois.","ceo_bio":"Mr. J. Patrick Gallagher Jr. | Chairman & CEO | Age 73 | Compensation: $11.7M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 69K people. Revenue per employee of $202K ranks in the bottom quartile among Financial Services peers, with revenue growing 14%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $26K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $710 per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 58\u00d7 revenue per employee (elevated relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (7/10).","financial_summary":["Arthur J. Gallagher & Co. is a large-cap financial services business with a $72.6B market cap on $13.9B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +18% over the past three years and +10% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 7% against a 7% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $1.8B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 13 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.29\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 3.5\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and interest coverage runs at 3.9\u00d7.","Net dilution runs at 1.1% annually, transferring value from owners to stock-based comp, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 31% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 2 other valuation measures)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.3067664249585547},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.4) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Operating margins 11% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $29.2M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Financial Services peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["37 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Arthur J. Gallagher (AJG) Posted Stronger Q3 Results, Is The Stock Fully Priced?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/insurance/nyse-ajg/arthur-j-gallagher/news/arthur-j-gallagher-ajg-posted-stronger-q3-results-is-the-sto","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794486408.082,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.914,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Arthur J. Gallagher & Co. $AJG Shares Sold by King Luther Capital Management Corp","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/12/arthur-j-gallagher-co-ajg-shares-sold-by-king-luther-capital-management-corp.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794483090.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.906,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Arthur J. Gallagher & Co. $AJG Shares Sold by Private Management Group Inc.","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/11/arthur-j-gallagher-co-ajg-shares-sold-by-private-management-group-inc.html","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794394302.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.84,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Arthur J. Gallagher (AJG) Stock Looks Undervalued With Excess Returns Still Strong","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/insurance/nyse-ajg/arthur-j-gall